          // now reach ~9.8 rad by the page bottom, 0.0004 gives ~2.1 rad,
          // continuing at roughly the ramp's own pace.
          continuous: { rotationYDelta: 0.0004 },
          ownsPosition: heroStillRelevant,
          // positionBase/cameraZ/fov are DOM/viewport measurements, not
          // functions of `t` (canvas offset depends on live CSS custom
          // properties; FOV on viewport width) — see particle-scroll-
          // director.js's own doc on why these go through `frame()` rather
          // than plain keyframe channels: returning null once no longer
          // relevant is what lets some LATER section's own camera reset
          // stick, instead of this zone re-asserting a stale zoomed value
          // for as long as _zoneActive()'s generous margin keeps it live.
          frame: (l, t) => {
            if (!heroStillRelevant()) return null;
            // UP-ONLY on scroll (2026-08-30, explicit request): no
            // horizontal drift and no downward dip. Previously this eased
            // BOTH axes toward Lab's entrance position ([0, -6, 0]) so the
            // handover never jumped — x drifted from the hero's left
            // canvas offset toward 0 (read as moving RIGHT), and y was
            // pulled from its risen position back DOWN to -6 (read as
            // moving DOWN) via a smoothstep blend keyed off the removed
            // CENTER_BY/LAB_ENTRY_Y constants. Removing that drift means
            // the Lab handoff may now snap/jump instead of being
            // seamless — accepted tradeoff, chosen over reintroducing
            // either direction of drift.
            if (t < EXIT_SPAN) {
              const off = l._getHeroCanvasOffset();
              const frac = Math.min(1, t / EXIT_SPAN);
              const zoomedZ = heroBaseCameraZ * ZOOM_FACTOR;
